Parity gap: the Parity Principle (AUR-CANONICAL-001 §VIII) requires the
external Node MCP decision core and the in-process Python twin to produce
bit-for-bit identical decisions. That comparison currently cannot run in
this repository — see parity/run_parity.py — because the Node core it
depends on is not vendored here. Until it is, parity is asserted by
doctrine, not verified by this repository's own tooling.
